^{:go/end 316} (go/method bitCounts "bitCounts returns an integer slice in which slice[i] is the number\nof literals that should be encoded using i bits.\n\nThis method is only called when len(list) >= 3.\nThe cases of 0, 1, and 2 literals are handled by special case code.\n\nlist is an array of the literals with non-zero frequencies\nand their associated frequencies. The array is in order of increasing\nfrequency and has as its last element a special element with frequency\nMaxInt32.\n\nmaxBits is the maximum number of bits that should be used to encode any literal.\nIt must be less than 16.\n" ^{:tag (slice int32)} [^{:tag (* huffmanEncoder)} h ^{:tag (slice literalNode)} list ^int32 maxBits]
